-- The shop's items that were not on the site yet (2026-11-27; owner: "We need all of the store's items on the site asap,
-- if there's issues let's get around them"). Two parts, each exactly what `catalog.py seed` writes (store/tools/catalog/
-- test_catalog.py checks they still match). Safe to run twice: new items are inserted once; an existing item's UPDATE only
-- fires when one of its supplier columns differs (none do: the 28 bowls and 31 hoses already live are unchanged by it).
-- Needs the new photos in store/public/img/pc/bowl/ deployed with the same commit (the light blue hose has no photo yet: it
-- shows "Photo coming soon" until the shop uploads one in the item editor). Run after
-- shop-photos-2026-11-27.sql and before any later live file that changes hose or bowl rows (this file re-seeds every
-- shop hose and bowl with "only if different" updates, so run after a newer one it would put these values back).
-- 1. Bowls (store/catalog/suppliers/shop-bowls/master.json): 37 of the shop's bowls with no brand printed on them, in 18
--    families, OSS-130029 to OSS-130065, section Bowls, Price TBD, in the shop, stock not counted, the shop's own cut-out
--    photo. Each has a plain name that only describes the photo; every one is flagged for the back office's Needs info list.
-- 2. Hoses (store/catalog/suppliers/shop-hoses/master.json): the Starbuzz Ribbed Hose in light blue, OSS-120032, from the
--    shop's counter photo "Star buzz are 76.5 inches"; flagged to check it is still in stock.
-- Rollback. First check nothing has been sold: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM order_items WHERE sku IN (SKUS); if that is not 0, do not
-- delete: UPDATE products SET listed = 0, active = 0 WHERE sku IN (SKUS). Otherwise (this also drops any shelf count, photo
-- upload, favourite or back-in-stock alert made on them since):
